# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps three things OUT
# of the image entirely.

# 1. THE DATABASE. data/fuel_tracker.db is still tracked in git — the real fuel
#    record, six fills and a year of HVAC reports. It must never be baked into
#    an image or shipped to a server as a code artifact. The live data lives in
#    Postgres; the repo carries schema, never data.
data/

# 2. SECRETS. The real .env must never enter the build context: anything copied
#    into a layer is recoverable from the image even if a later layer deletes
#    it. .env.example is a template and is fine, but is not needed either.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# 3. HOST-PLATFORM BINARIES. node_modules built on macOS cannot run on Linux,
#    and copying them in would shadow the on-target npm ci.
node_modules
**/node_modules
*/dist
dist

# Everything below is noise that only slows the build and busts layer caches.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
Documentation
*.md
!README.md
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
